        "original_id": "8c6ea14d-1ff8-5689-8a6b-dcc637200d96",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Sentinelese people\n- Places: North Sentinel Island, Andaman and Nicobar Islands, Andaman Islands, South Sentinel Island, Bay of Bengal, India\n- Languages: Sentinelese language, Andamanese languages\n- Concepts: uncontacted peoples, language classification\n\nFacts:\n- North Sentinel Island is one of the Andaman Islands in the Bay of Bengal, and the Andaman Islands include South Sentinel Island.\n- The Sentinelese people live on North Sentinel Island in the Andaman and Nicobar Islands of India.\n- Sentinelese is the presumed language of the Sentinelese people.\n- The Sentinelese language is the language of an uncontacted people and is therefore currently unclassifiable within the Andamanese languages context.",
